    (0x5ac9ec, 'function', 'FrameEarlyUpdate', 'FrameEarlyUpdate [medium] Early update called from FrameBegin with dt60=G[624]*60/G[614] | src: notes/frame-timing.md §1 Loop diagram'),
    (0x5acaaa, 'label', 'FrameEarlyUpdate_CallPadStageWait', 'FrameEarlyUpdate_CallPadStageWait [high] call InputWorkerWaitPadStage 86C018 (<=1 ms wait for the pad stage) at the START of the logic frame, before GameModeUpdateMain consumes the pad. Site C / IKc: IK moves the input kick here (E8 69 F5 2B 00) | src: notes/input-latency.md §2; patcher/latency_live.fsx'),
    (0x5acee8, 'function', 'FrameTask_Update', 'FrameTask_Update [high] FrameTask vtable 0x40358E8 vf[1] (verified live); calls dt setup 0x5AD5F8 then tail-jmps to FrameEnd 0x5ACF80 (aka GameMainTick) || also: Caller of GameFrameUpdate (152 B, 0 direct callers, so reached via vtable/callback) | sig: void FrameTask::Update(FrameTask* this) | src: notes/frame-timing.md §1 Loop diagram, §4b; re/out/README.md §Findings: frame pacing'),
    (0x5acf80, 'function', 'FrameEnd', 'FrameEnd [high] Frame end (tail-jmp target of 0x5ACEE8): frameskip flag test 0x5AD0BA, per-scene updates (vtbl +40 lists), QPC busy-wait limiter 0x5AD229..0x5AD2BB (+cold 0x19DF57E), measured interval [r15+24], game clock [r13+3BFBC] += [r15+18] (aka FrameStepAndLimit) || also: per-frame step run on KIDSTaskScheduler0; its pacing tail is the frame limiter = Sleep(0)+job-poll busy-wait until the frame deadline (W4/S4); up to 0.4-0.7 core when frames have slack [Ghidra: 1734 B, 1 callers] | sig: void FrameEnd(...) | src: notes/frame-timing.md §1, §3; notes/cpu-profile.md §S4; §TL;DR W4'),
    (0x5ad0ba, 'label', 'FrameEnd_FrameskipTest', 'FrameEnd_FrameskipTest [high] Frameskip flag test profile+2C & 0x8000 -> ctx[200] OR= 2; Lyall Nioh3Fix 0.0.2 Frameskip sig start (option removed in 0.0.4) | src: notes/frame-timing.md §1, §3; notes/fps-unlock-research.md §1'),
